To compare our algorithm with skyline reducing algorithms, we have implemented the algorithms KRSPG REEDY [3 cuisine-based on a binary relation of attributes and their values. The regret ratio is computed as follows: 

The regret ratio score for each point in the output set is calculated by comparing it to the global minima (the best possible representative) using the following formula:

Regret Ratio = (1 - Quality(URM)) / (Quality of Optimal Choice - Quality of URM Output)/(Time Budget/Total Time). 

The regret ratio is a measure of how much worse our algorithm's output is compared to the global minima. The lower the regret ratio, the better. For instance, if the score for an item in the skyline is 10 and URM outputs a representative with a score of 95, then its regret ratio would be (1 - 95/100) = 5%.

The regret ratio scores reduce monotonically as time passes. This means that it produces better results as time passes. In contrast, GREEDY-SHRINK generates results only at program termination and does not provide any output until the end of the time budget. Therefore, in order to make a fair assessment, we run the HD-RRMS algorithm with different values 
